BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cannes-residence-cinema-de-demain-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T182657Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: La Résidence du Festival de Cannes (Cinéma de Demain): 
 Screenwriting Residency in Paris
DESCRIPTION:La Résidence of the Festival de Cannes (part of Cinéma de Dem
 ain\, formerly La Cinéfondation) invites 12 directors each year to write 
 their screenplay in Paris. The programme provides a place of residence in 
 the heart of Paris\, a personalised programme accompanying the writing of 
 their scripts\, and a collective programme of forums with film industry pr
 ofessionals. The 12 directors from the two annual sessions present their p
 rojects at the CNC pavilion in Cannes\, giving 10-minute presentations to 
 an audience of professionals and a jury of three film industry personaliti
 es\; the CNC then awards a EUR 5\,000 grant to one director from each sess
 ion\, based on the project that most inspires the jury. The Cinef & Résid
 ence offices serve as a hub where directors meet and schedule private meet
 ings with potential producers. ELIGIBILITY: open to young filmmakers who h
 ave made one or several short films and no more than one feature film\; ca
 ndidates must NOT be residents or citizens of France. Selected filmmakers 
 must stay at the Résidence in Paris for the full session. SESSIONS: two p
 er year\, each lasting four and a half months\, the first running 15 March
  to 31 July and the second 1 October to 15 February. Artistic fields: film
 \, writing\, interdisciplinary. Deadline: 30 September 2026 at 16:00 UTC. 
 Free to apply.\n\nOrganisation: Festival de Cannes (Cinéma de Demain / La
  Résidence)\nLocation: Paris\, France. Candidates must not be residents o
 r citizens of France.\nAward: Fully supported: a place of residence in cen
 tral Paris\, a personalised script-writing programme\, and a collective pr
 ogramme of forums with film industry professionals. Directors present at t
 he CNC pavilion in Cannes\, where the CNC awards a EUR 5\,000 grant to one
  director per session. Free to apply.\nDuration: Four and a half months pe
 r session (two sessions a year)\n\nMore: https://cinemadedemain.festival-c
 annes.com/en/take-part/register-to-the-residence/?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://cinemadedemain.festival-cannes.com/en/take-part/register-to-the
 -residence/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Paris\, France. Candidates must not be residents or citizens of Fr
 ance.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:berlinale-talents-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260823T182657Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260902
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260903
SUMMARY:Deadline: Berlinale Talents 2027 (Berlin International Film Festiva
 l)
DESCRIPTION:Berlinale Talents is the Berlin International Film Festival's t
 alent-development program: a week of workshops\, the Talents Lab and the T
 alent Project Market during the February 2027 Berlinale\, plus access to t
 he festival's industry network. ELIGIBILITY: international working film pr
 ofessionals with at least 1 feature\, 2 shorts\, or a widely screened or s
 treamed series\, across 15+ disciplines including directing\, sound design
 \, editing\, production\, cinematography and screenwriting. Participation 
 itself is free\; there is a EUR 15 application service fee (EUR 10 early b
 ird before 19 August 2026) and travel and accommodation are not covered. D
 eadline 2 September 2026\, 12:00 CEST. Apply via the Berlinale Talents por
 tal.\n\nOrganisation: Berlinale / Berlin International Film Festival\nLoca
 tion: Berlin\, Germany (during the Berlinale\, February 2027)\; open inter
 nationally.\nAward: Free participation in the week-long professional progr
 am (Summit workshops\, Talents Lab\, Talent Project Market\, industry netw
 orking). NO stipend\; travel and accommodation are self-covered (national 
 film institutes often fund this\; Netherlands-based filmmakers can approac
 h the Netherlands Film Fund). EUR 15 application service fee (EUR 10 early
  bird before 19 August 2026).\nDuration: One week during the Berlinale\, F
 ebruary 2027\n\nMore: https://www.berlinale-talents.de/bt/page/c/apply?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.berlinale-talents.de/bt/page/c/apply?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berlin\, Germany (during the Berlinale\, February 2027)\; open int
 ernationally.
END:VEVENT
